---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const structuredData = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Person",
    "@id": "https://draayushshrestha.com/#doctor",
    name: "Dr. Aayush Shrestha",
    honorificPrefix: "Dr.",
    jobTitle: "Orthopaedic and Spine Surgeon",
    description: "Orthopaedic and spine surgeon practising in Kathmandu and Lalitpur, Nepal.",
    url: "https://draayushshrestha.com/about.html",
    image: "https://draayushshrestha.com/assets/images/doctor-white-coat.jpg",
    telephone: "+977-9841382407",
    email: "draayushshrestha@gmail.com",
    alumniOf: [
      { "@type": "EducationalOrganization", name: "University of Dhaka" },
      { "@type": "EducationalOrganization", name: "Kathmandu University" },
    ],
    worksFor: [
      { "@type": "Hospital", name: "Grande International Hospital" },
      { "@id": "https://draayushshrestha.com/#pacific-clinic" },
    ],
    knowsAbout: ["Orthopaedic surgery", "Spine surgery", "Endoscopic spine surgery"],
    sameAs: ["https://www.instagram.com/orthopedics.spine/", "https://youtube.com/@dr.AayushShrestha", "https://www.linkedin.com/in/dr-aayush-shrestha-b7b044165"],
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "WebSite",
    "@id": "https://draayushshrestha.com/#website",
    url: "https://draayushshrestha.com/",
    name: "Dr. Aayush Shrestha",
    inLanguage: "en",
    publisher: { "@id": "https://draayushshrestha.com/#doctor" },
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Orthopaedic & Spine Surgeon in Nepal | Dr. Aayush Shrestha"
  description="Consult Dr. Aayush Shrestha, an orthopaedic and spine surgeon in Kathmandu and Lalitpur, Nepal. Explore conditions and appointments."
  canonical="https://draayushshrestha.com/"
  active="home"
  structuredData={structuredData}
>

  <main id="main">
    <section class="hero"><div class="shell hero__grid"><div class="hero__copy"><p class="kicker">Kathmandu &amp; Lalitpur, Nepal</p><h1>Orthopaedic care, explained clearly.</h1><p class="hero__lede">Dr. Aayush Shrestha evaluates bone, joint and spine conditions with an emphasis on clear diagnosis, appropriate non-operative care and surgery when indicated.</p><div class="hero__actions"><a class="btn btn--primary" href="contact.html">Book appointment</a><a class="btn" href="conditions.html">Explore conditions</a></div></div><figure class="hero__portrait"><img src="assets/images/doctor-white-coat.jpg" width="1024" height="1280" fetchpriority="high" alt="Dr. Aayush Shrestha in a white medical coat"><figcaption class="hero__caption">Orthopaedic and spine consultations in Kathmandu and Lalitpur.</figcaption></figure></div></section>

    <section class="credential-strip" aria-label="Professional overview"><ul class="shell"><li><strong>MBBS, MS Orthopaedics</strong><span>Medical and postgraduate surgical training</span></li><li><strong>Spine surgery fellowship</strong><span>Focused training in spine care</span></li><li><strong>Surgical and non-operative care</strong><span>Treatment matched to diagnosis and need</span></li></ul></section>

    <section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="section-head"><h2>A focused clinical practice</h2><p>Patients seek care for back and neck pain, fractures, joint problems, sports injuries and other musculoskeletal conditions. The first task is not to choose a procedure. It is to understand the problem.</p></div><div class="split"><div class="split__copy"><h3>Spine care</h3><p>Assessment and treatment for back pain, neck pain, sciatica, disc problems, spinal stenosis, deformity, trauma and other spine conditions.</p><ul class="fact-list"><li>Clinical examination and imaging review</li><li>Non-operative treatment where appropriate</li><li>Decompression, fusion and minimally invasive options when indicated</li></ul><a class="text-link" href="conditions.html#spine">View spine conditions →</a></div><figure class="split__media"><img src="assets/images/conference-presentation.jpg" width="1600" height="1066" loading="lazy" alt="Dr. Aayush Shrestha presenting on spinal surgery"></figure></div><div class="split split--reverse"><div class="split__copy"><h3>Orthopaedic care</h3><p>Evaluation of painful joints, fractures, soft-tissue injuries and mobility problems, with treatment ranging from rehabilitation and medication to surgery.</p><ul class="fact-list"><li>Knee, shoulder, hip and upper-limb conditions</li><li>Trauma and fracture management</li><li>Rehabilitation and return-to-activity planning</li></ul><a class="text-link" href="conditions.html#joints">View orthopaedic conditions →</a></div><figure class="split__media"><img src="assets/images/knee-pain.jpg" width="1200" height="675" loading="lazy" alt="Person holding a painful knee"></figure></div></div></section>

    <section class="section section--paper-2"><div class="shell"><div class="section-head"><h2>Hospital and clinic affiliations</h2><p>Dr. Shrestha’s current website identifies these organisations as practice affiliations. Contact each facility for current schedules and appointment availability.</p></div><div class="logo-wall logo-wall--large"><ul><li><img src="assets/images/grande-hospital.png" width="500" height="500" alt="Grande International Hospital"></li><li><img src="assets/images/pacific-clinic.png" width="500" height="500" alt="Pacific Multispeciality Clinic"></li><li><img src="assets/images/shankhamul-healthcare.png" width="892" height="893" alt="Shankhamul Healthcare"></li></ul></div></div></section>

    <section class="section section--dark"><div class="shell"><div class="section-head"><h2>Start with where it hurts</h2><p>Use this guide to understand common condition groups. It does not replace an examination or diagnosis.</p></div><div class="body-map"><a href="conditions.html#spine"><strong>Back &amp; spine</strong><span>Disc, nerve, stenosis, deformity</span></a><a href="conditions.html#neck"><strong>Neck</strong><span>Pain, stiffness, arm symptoms</span></a><a href="conditions.html#joints"><strong>Knee &amp; hip</strong><span>Arthritis, injury, mobility</span></a><a href="conditions.html#upper-limb"><strong>Shoulder &amp; elbow</strong><span>Tendon, instability, trauma</span></a><a href="conditions.html#hand-foot"><strong>Hand, wrist &amp; foot</strong><span>Nerve, tendon, joint pain</span></a><a href="conditions.html#trauma"><strong>Trauma</strong><span>Fractures and dislocations</span></a></div></div></section>

    <section class="section"><div class="narrow"><p class="kicker">Patient perspective</p><div class="quote"><blockquote>“He takes his time examining and makes the patient understand the situation.”</blockquote><cite>Arjesh Karmacharya · patient testimonial</cite><a class="text-link" href="about.html#reviews">Read patient experiences →</a></div></div></section>

    <section class="section section--paper-2"><div class="shell"><div class="section-head"><h2>Patient guides</h2><p>Practical starting points for spine, joint and post-operative questions. General education cannot account for your individual diagnosis.</p></div><div class="article-grid"><article class="article-card"><p class="kicker">Danger signs</p><h3>Signs of nerve compression in the neck</h3><p>When neck pain, arm symptoms or loss of function needs prompt assessment.</p><a class="text-link" href="patient-guides.html#spine-guide">Read the guide →</a></article><article class="article-card"><p class="kicker">Joint health</p><h3>Maintaining healthy knees</h3><p>Weight, movement, footwear and safer loading.</p><a class="text-link" href="patient-guides.html#knee-guide">Read the guide →</a></article><article class="article-card"><p class="kicker">Myths &amp; facts</p><h3>Understanding disc herniation</h3><p>Symptoms, treatment and when surgery may not be required.</p><a class="text-link" href="patient-guides.html#spine-guide">Read the guide →</a></article></div></div></section>

    <section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="section-head"><h2>Choosing an orthopaedic doctor in Nepal</h2><p>Search rankings and superlatives cannot identify the right doctor for every patient. Look for relevant specialist training, hospital affiliations, a clear explanation of options and a treatment plan matched to your condition.</p></div><div class="faq"><details><summary>Who is the best orthopaedic doctor in Nepal?</summary><p>There is no objective single “best” doctor for every orthopaedic problem. Choose a specialist whose training and current practice match your condition, verify credentials and affiliations, and seek a second opinion for major surgery when appropriate.</p></details><details><summary>Do all spine problems require surgery?</summary><p>No. Many conditions can be managed with activity modification, medication, physiotherapy or other non-operative care. Surgery is considered when diagnosis, symptoms, examination and response to treatment support it.</p></details><details><summary>What should I bring to an appointment?</summary><p>Bring previous prescriptions, reports, X-rays or MRI/CT images, a list of medicines and a short timeline of your symptoms. Note any weakness, numbness, fever, recent injury or changes in bladder or bowel control.</p></details></div></div></section>

    <section class="section section--dark"><div class="shell cta-band"><h2>Bring the problem. Leave with a clearer plan.</h2><div><p>Clinic appointments in Kupondole, Lalitpur.</p><p class="action-block"><a class="btn btn--light" href="contact.html">View appointment details</a></p></div></div></section>
  </main>

</BaseLayout>
